From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram with more than one write port
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

generate_ram took exactly one read/write or one write port (RAM-0030).
It now takes any number of write ports: each has its own address
decoder, data bus (D0, D1, ...), write enables (we0, we1, ...) and
address (addr_w0, addr_w1, ...); one write port keeps the names it had.
Per word, port w writes when its row select and write enable are high;
a word written by two ports in a cycle keeps the last one's data, as
the behavioral model does; the word's clock gate opens for any of them.
Per bit an AO22 per pair of ports, and an OR2 across pairs, picks the
data. The AO22 is found by its truth table, as the AOI22 is, through
findMaster4, which both now share; the OR2 by its function.

Not yet with -use_latch, whose data passes a latch per column, or with
-column_mux_ratio above 1, whose word select comes from the first
port's address (RAM-0054, RAM-0055).

Tested: src/ram/test/write_ports_nangate45.tcl.

Commit 1 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
